WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.764
Welcome to The BEE Suite.

00:00:01.764 --> 00:00:03.527
Welcome to The BEE Suite.

00:00:03.527 --> 00:00:09.876
This tour explains what each director section is for and where to go when a task comes up.

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:15.872
We will move from the school day to families, billing, staff, records, enrollment, reports, setup and support.

00:00:15.872 --> 00:00:21.515
This is an illustrated navigation walkthrough with synthetic screen examples, not a demonstration of live changes.

00:00:21.515 --> 00:00:26.100
After the tour, use the individual task lessons to learn the detailed steps.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:28.372
Find your way around.

00:00:28.372 --> 00:00:30.579
First check your school and role.

00:00:30.579 --> 00:00:36.835
The main menu takes you to a workspace, and the tabs within that workspace narrow the task.

00:00:36.835 --> 00:00:41.250
For example, Families and Communication contains Families, Children, Messages and Media review.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:44.929
Your menu depends on your role, brand and enabled features.

00:00:44.929 --> 00:00:49.345
On a phone, use the menu or More to reach additional sections.

00:00:49.345 --> 00:00:56.704
The navigation map in this lesson groups destinations for learning; it is not an exact copy of every account's menu.

00:00:57.504 --> 00:00:57.868
Dashboard.

00:00:57.868 --> 00:00:59.691
Start the day on Dashboard.

00:00:59.691 --> 00:01:06.983
It is the overview of your school, with the items that need attention and routes into the work behind them.

00:01:06.983 --> 00:01:13.181
Use it to decide what to investigate next: classroom coverage, attendance, family follow-up or an outstanding exception.

00:01:13.181 --> 00:01:15.368
A summary is a starting point.

00:01:15.368 --> 00:01:20.108
Open the relevant workspace and check the actual record before making a change.

00:01:20.108 --> 00:01:23.754
Return here during the day to review priorities and follow-up.

00:01:24.554 --> 00:01:25.358
School Operations.

00:01:25.358 --> 00:01:28.172
School Operations is for the school day.

00:01:28.172 --> 00:01:30.986
Enrollment status shows the roster and exports.

00:01:30.986 --> 00:01:34.203
Classrooms is for rooms, capacity, ratios and activity.

00:01:34.203 --> 00:01:37.017
Attendance is for arrival and departure status.

00:01:37.017 --> 00:01:43.449
Daily reports covers care notes and family updates, while Incidents is for safety records and follow-up.

00:01:43.449 --> 00:01:49.480
The teacher screen shown here is a synthetic example of the classroom work directors oversee.

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:54.304
Check the child, classroom and date before reviewing or correcting a record.

00:01:55.104 --> 00:01:56.302
Families & Communication.

00:01:56.302 --> 00:02:00.296
Families and Communication brings together household records and family conversations.

00:02:00.296 --> 00:02:03.491
Use Families for guardians, household details and contacts.

00:02:03.491 --> 00:02:07.086
Use Children for child profiles, care information and permissions.

00:02:07.086 --> 00:02:12.678
Use Messages for family conversations, and Media review for photo review and sharing decisions.

00:02:12.678 --> 00:02:19.867
If a parent reports the wrong phone number or needs a sibling added, start with the existing family.

00:02:19.867 --> 00:02:26.657
If you need to investigate an account balance, move to Billing and Payments for that same family.

00:02:27.457 --> 00:02:28.641
Billing & Payments.

00:02:28.641 --> 00:02:33.769
Billing and Payments is the home for tuition, invoices, balances and payment follow-up.

00:02:33.769 --> 00:02:38.108
Billing and invoices is where you review family accounts and charges.

00:02:38.108 --> 00:02:40.870
Payments is for transaction review and reconciliation.

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:47.182
Keep the questions separate: what tuition is assigned, what invoice exists, and what payment actually happened?

00:02:47.182 --> 00:02:51.915
A saved payment method, autopay setting and paid invoice are different states.

00:02:51.915 --> 00:02:59.411
Use the billing task lessons for the exact procedure, and check the result before repeating an uncertain payment action.

00:03:00.211 --> 00:03:01.284
Staff & Access.

00:03:01.284 --> 00:03:05.220
Staff and Access is for the people working at your school.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:12.376
The Teachers view contains staff records and classroom assignments, with the staff management tools used for schedules and time cards.

00:03:12.376 --> 00:03:18.101
Team permissions is the place to review roles and module access where your account permits it.

00:03:18.101 --> 00:03:22.394
Review the employee and the relevant date before correcting a time entry.

00:03:22.394 --> 00:03:28.835
Changing a profile, changing classroom coverage and granting access are separate tasks; use the appropriate procedure for each.

00:03:29.635 --> 00:03:30.850
Records & Compliance.

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:33.280
Records and Compliance organizes required paperwork.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:35.306
Forms covers templates and submissions.

00:03:35.306 --> 00:03:37.736
Documents is for files and acknowledgements.

00:03:37.736 --> 00:03:40.977
Compliance brings together tasks, evidence and readiness information.

00:03:40.977 --> 00:03:47.458
Start here when you need a required document or need to see what is still missing.

00:03:47.458 --> 00:03:52.319
Verify the intended family or staff member, the document and its status.

00:03:52.319 --> 00:03:57.585
A request being created is different from a submission being received and reviewed.

00:03:58.385 --> 00:03:59.143
Enrollment CRM.

00:03:59.143 --> 00:04:03.696
Enrollment CRM is for prospective families and the process leading to enrollment.

00:04:03.696 --> 00:04:06.731
Leads is the inbox and lead record area.

00:04:06.731 --> 00:04:08.628
Pipeline shows stages and progress.

00:04:08.628 --> 00:04:10.904
Tours is for scheduling and follow-up.

00:04:10.904 --> 00:04:13.180
Waitlist helps track demand and openings.

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:16.974
Use this workspace before a family becomes an enrolled household.

00:04:16.974 --> 00:04:29.493
When the process reaches enrollment, verify the actual family and child records and the enrollment status; moving a lead stage alone should not be treated as proof that every onboarding task is complete.

00:04:30.293 --> 00:04:31.089
FTE reports.

00:04:31.089 --> 00:04:34.271
FTE reports is the dedicated weekly reporting workspace.

00:04:34.271 --> 00:04:42.625
Select the intended school and reporting week, check the counts and notes, and use the submission or correction process shown there.

00:04:42.625 --> 00:04:46.603
It is different from simply exporting the current enrollment roster.

00:04:46.603 --> 00:04:50.979
After an authorized submission, verify the recorded result for that week.

00:04:50.979 --> 00:04:53.365
Executive review is a separate step.

00:04:53.365 --> 00:04:57.343
Use the FTE task lesson for the detailed reporting procedure.

00:04:58.143 --> 00:04:59.363
Insights & Reputation.

00:04:59.363 --> 00:05:03.429
Insights and Reputation is for reports, trends and family feedback.

00:05:03.429 --> 00:05:07.902
Enrollment status is another route to the roster and its exports.

00:05:07.902 --> 00:05:11.155
Analytics helps you review operating metrics and trends.

00:05:11.155 --> 00:05:14.002
Reputation is for reviews and family sentiment.

00:05:14.002 --> 00:05:18.475
Check the school, filters and time period before interpreting a result.

00:05:18.475 --> 00:05:26.607
Reports help you spot a question; return to the underlying family, classroom, enrollment or billing record to investigate the detail.

00:05:27.407 --> 00:05:28.633
Campaigns & Automations.

00:05:28.633 --> 00:05:32.719
Campaigns and Automations is for planned outreach and workflow configuration.

00:05:32.719 --> 00:05:36.396
Use Campaigns to review the audience and campaign content.

00:05:36.396 --> 00:05:40.482
Use Automations to inspect triggers, conditions and intended follow-up steps.

00:05:40.482 --> 00:05:44.977
This differs from answering one family's message in Families and Communication.

00:05:44.977 --> 00:05:50.288
Saving a workflow configuration does not prove that it runs or sends anything.

00:05:50.288 --> 00:05:56.826
Confirm the supported execution and review process before expecting a real message or other external action.

00:05:57.626 --> 00:05:59.027
AI Command and Mr.

00:05:59.027 --> 00:05:59.377
Bee.

00:05:59.377 --> 00:06:01.129
AI Command and the Mr.

00:06:01.129 --> 00:06:04.632
Bee entry point provide assistance with information, summaries and drafts.

00:06:04.632 --> 00:06:08.836
Use them to understand a task, organize a follow-up or prepare wording.

00:06:08.836 --> 00:06:11.988
Review the source record and the proposed result yourself.

00:06:11.988 --> 00:06:17.593
An AI response is not proof that a school record changed or a message was delivered.

00:06:17.593 --> 00:06:24.950
For any supported action, check the exact target and confirmation, then verify the result in the workspace that owns that record.

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:27.067
Settings & Setup.

00:06:27.067 --> 00:06:31.020
Settings and Setup holds school preferences and setup work.

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:33.655
Settings contains billing and school preferences.

00:06:33.655 --> 00:06:36.730
Integrations is where connected services are reviewed.

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:42.439
School setup is for the school profile, data starting point and readiness steps.

00:06:42.439 --> 00:06:45.075
Notifications contains alert and delivery preferences.

00:06:45.075 --> 00:06:50.784
Some options require additional permissions; for example, White-label branding is an executive view.

00:06:50.784 --> 00:06:56.055
Completing setup, connecting a service and approving school launch are separate decisions.

00:06:56.055 --> 00:07:00.007
Use the setup checklist and the matching task guide.

00:07:00.807 --> 00:07:02.372
Data readiness, when enabled.

00:07:02.372 --> 00:07:06.675
When enabled for your school, Data readiness helps organize data review.

00:07:06.675 --> 00:07:11.370
It belongs with the School setup work, especially when transitioning existing records.

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:16.847
Check families, guardian relationships, enrollment, tuition and opening balances against the approved source information.

00:07:16.847 --> 00:07:20.759
A completed import is not the same as verified records.

00:07:20.759 --> 00:07:30.930
If the separate Data readiness entry is not visible, use the School setup guidance available to your account and ask support about the intended review process.

00:07:31.730 --> 00:07:33.519
BEES and training resources.

00:07:33.519 --> 00:07:39.781
For Kid City USA management accounts, BEES opens the director and owner resource area.

00:07:39.781 --> 00:07:46.937
It includes links to leadership resources, school forms, curriculum materials, employee training, menus and manager training.

00:07:46.937 --> 00:07:50.515
Linked Drive folders enforce their own access permissions.

00:07:50.515 --> 00:07:54.541
The Resources area also provides the director tutorial library.

00:07:54.541 --> 00:07:57.671
Use these reference materials alongside the workspaces.

00:07:57.671 --> 00:08:04.380
Confirm the currently required reporting destination before substituting an external form for an in-suite workflow.

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:05.947
Asset Hub.

00:08:05.947 --> 00:08:10.929
Asset Hub is the library for approved brand, social, training and school resources.

00:08:10.929 --> 00:08:17.060
Search or filter the library, preview the correct item and download it for the intended use.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:23.959
Director access is primarily about finding and using the available resources; upload and management controls depend on role.

00:08:23.959 --> 00:08:27.024
Downloading an asset does not publish it anywhere.

00:08:27.024 --> 00:08:31.240
Use your school's approved process when sharing or publishing the material.

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:33.610
Notifications and Audit logs.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:36.751
Notifications brings attention to items that need follow-up.

00:08:36.751 --> 00:08:40.285
Open the related record and verify its current state.

00:08:40.285 --> 00:08:48.137
Audit logs, also described as activity history, helps review recorded actions: who acted, what happened and which record was involved.

00:08:48.137 --> 00:08:51.278
It supports investigation when a change is unclear.

00:08:51.278 --> 00:09:00.309
An activity entry is evidence of what was recorded; it is not automatically proof of email delivery, bank settlement or a person's acknowledgement.

00:09:01.109 --> 00:09:02.246
Help and support.

00:09:02.246 --> 00:09:06.038
Help is the place to look for instructions and troubleshooting.

00:09:06.038 --> 00:09:08.692
Start with the guide for your task.

00:09:08.692 --> 00:09:16.275
If you still need support, describe the school, the task, the time, the exact error and the result you expected.

00:09:16.275 --> 00:09:18.550
Include a safe screenshot when useful.

00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:21.963
Avoid including passwords, private credentials or unnecessary family information.

00:09:21.963 --> 00:09:28.409
The goal is to give support enough context to identify the correct record and reproduce the issue.

00:09:29.209 --> 00:09:31.584
Family kiosk, staff clock and portals.

00:09:31.584 --> 00:09:35.940
The suite also has experiences for families, teachers and kiosk users.

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:41.880
The family kiosk supports arrival and pickup, and the staff kiosk supports clock-in and clock-out.

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:44.651
Teachers work in their own classroom workspace.

00:09:44.651 --> 00:09:50.987
Parents use their own linked portal for family information, messages and billing features available to them.

00:09:50.987 --> 00:09:56.530
Directors oversee these workflows and help troubleshoot, but should not use someone else's credentials.

00:09:56.530 --> 00:10:01.282
Use the separate kiosk, teacher and parent lessons for the detailed steps.

00:10:02.082 --> 00:10:04.073
Sections that depend on access.

00:10:04.073 --> 00:10:06.063
Some sections are intentionally role-specific.

00:10:06.063 --> 00:10:11.637
Terminal store appears only when enabled and is separate from taking a family payment.

00:10:11.637 --> 00:10:16.414
Multi-location, Executive admin, Software invoice and Developer are not standard director destinations.

00:10:16.414 --> 00:10:18.007
White-label is also restricted.

00:10:18.007 --> 00:10:22.784
A director should not expect to see every executive or platform control.

00:10:22.784 --> 00:10:31.145
If a section needed for your assigned work is missing, ask the authorized administrator to review the role and school scope.

00:10:31.945 --> 00:10:34.153
Choose the workspace by the task.

00:10:34.153 --> 00:10:36.360
Here is the route to remember.

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:38.936
A new inquiry goes to Enrollment CRM.

00:10:38.936 --> 00:10:41.879
A contact correction goes to Families and Communication.

00:10:41.879 --> 00:10:44.823
A balance question goes to Billing and Payments.

00:10:44.823 --> 00:10:48.134
A missed staff punch goes to Staff and Access.

00:10:48.134 --> 00:10:51.078
A missing form goes to Records and Compliance.

00:10:51.078 --> 00:10:54.021
For attendance and daily care, use School Operations.

00:10:54.021 --> 00:11:02.484
Start the day on Dashboard, work in the section that owns the task, verify the result, and use Help when something remains unclear.

00:11:02.484 --> 00:11:05.795
You are ready to move into the task tutorials.
